Package: wilai
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: WilOS <maintainer@wilos.example>
Homepage: https://github.com/dimita/os_windows
Depends: libc6, libxkbcommon0, systemd
Recommends: ollama | ollama-cuda, network-manager, pipewire, pipewire-pulse, alsa-utils, openssh-server, socat, python3, curl
Suggests: whisper-cpp, piper-tts, libnotify-bin, zenity, grim, scrot, nmap, nuclei, whatweb
Description: Wilai — local, auditable system agent (AI shell for Linux)
 Wilai is an on-device AI agent that drives a Linux system through
 typed, YAML-declared tools. Every tool call is confirmed and recorded
 in a tamper-evident hash-chained audit log. The default LLM provider
 is a local Ollama instance; the security.local_only lock refuses any
 non-local provider.
 .
 This package installs:
   * wilai-daemon — the long-running agent service (system unit)
   * wilai-shell  — full-screen TUI frontend (tty + SSH drop-shell)
   * wilai-hud    — Wayland layer-shell HUD overlay (user unit)
   * wilai        — command-line client
   * wilai-voice, wilai-overlay — optional voice + desktop toasts
   * sys.* / memory.* / remote.* / vision.* YAML tool catalogue
 .
 Three ways to use Wilai after install:
   1. Run `wilai` from your terminal.
   2. SSH into the machine as the `wilai` user — you drop directly
      into the TUI (its login shell is wilai-shell).
   3. On Hyprland (or any wlroots compositor), enable the
      wilai-hud.service user unit for a permanent face HUD.
